            "image": "shopify://shop_images/adv-board-kapoor.webp",
            "name": "Dr Ash Kapoor · Biochemist, formulation science",
            "quote": "“We didn’t just look at NAD. We looked at how it’s produced, how it’s protected, and how it gets used.”",
            "note": "<p>That question is the whole reason he joined the advisory board, and it’s the order the list below is ranked in.</p>",
            "signature": "",
            "image_position": "left",
            "dark": false
          }
        },
        "head_rank": {
          "type": "section_head",
          "settings": {
            "label": "The ranking",
            "title": "Five that earn their place, in order.",
            "align": "center",
            "small": false,
            "tight": false
          }
        },
        "rank01": {
          "type": "rank",
          "settings": {
            "numeral": "01",
            "label": "Energy production",
            "title": "MUTO NAD⁺ Cellular Complex",
            "text": "<p>NAD⁺ is what mitochondria use to turn food into energy and what repair enzymes need to work at all. Levels fall steadily with age, so this is the input everything else in the list depends on.</p>",
            "aside_label": "Why it ranks first",
            "aside_text": "Production, protection and use are handled in one formula rather than left to chance across three.",
            "dark": true
          }
        },
        "rank02": {
          "type": "rank",
          "settings": {
            "numeral": "02",
            "label": "Hormone signalling",
            "title": "Vitamin D3",
            "text": "<p>Closer to a hormone than a vitamin, and involved in immune function, mood and bone health. In the UK there is no meaningful sun-derived supply for half the year.</p>",
            "aside_label": "How to buy it",
            "aside_text": "Taken with K2 and with a meal containing fat, otherwise most of it goes unabsorbed.",
            "dark": false
          }
        },
        "rank03": {
          "type": "rank",
          "settings": {
            "numeral": "03",
            "label": "Gut support",
            "title": "Probiotic",
            "text": "<p>Absorption is the step most stacks ignore. A supplement is only worth what the gut manages to take up, and gut health is the variable that decides it.</p>",
            "aside_label": "How to buy it",
            "aside_text": "Look for named strains and a CFU count on the label, not a blend description.",
            "dark": false
          }
        },
        "rank04": {
          "type": "rank",
          "settings": {
            "numeral": "04",
            "label": "Recovery and sleep",
            "title": "Magnesium",
            "text": "<p>A cofactor in hundreds of enzymatic reactions, including the ones that make and spend cellular energy. Training raises the demand for it; most diets don’t meet the baseline.</p>",
            "aside_label": "How to buy it",
            "aside_text": "The form matters more than the milligrams. Glycinate or malate, taken in the evening.",
            "dark": false
          }
        },
        "rank05": {
          "type": "rank",
          "settings": {
            "numeral": "05",
            "label": "Detoxification",
            "title": "Glutathione",
            "text": "<p>The body’s own antioxidant, used to clear the oxidative damage that hard training and ordinary metabolism generate. Production falls with age alongside NAD⁺.</p>",
            "aside_label": "How to buy it",
            "aside_text": "Liposomal or NAC as a precursor. Plain oral glutathione is largely broken down before it lands.",
            "dark": false
          }
        },
        "head_why": {
          "type": "section_head",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Why he worked with MUTO",
            "title": "Most NAD⁺ products answer one question out of three.",
            "align": "center",
            "small": false,
            "tight": false
          }
        },
        "lede_why": {
          "type": "lede",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Raising NAD⁺ is the easy part. What decides whether it does anything is what happens next: how much of it survives, and whether the cell has what it needs to spend it. A single-ingredient product leaves both of those unanswered.</p><p>MUTO is built around those three jobs - produce, protect, put to work. Every dose is at the level used in the research it comes from and printed in full on the label.</p>",
            "align": "left"
          }
        },
